%global debug_package %{nil}
%global __os_install_post %{nil}
%global _build_id_links none

Name:           amazon-music-linux
Version:        @VERSION@
Release:        1%{?dist}
Summary:        Node.js Amazon Music client with native GTK4/libadwaita and Electron
License:        MIT AND BSD-3-Clause AND LGPL-2.1-or-later
Source0:        %{name}-%{version}.tar.gz
AutoReqProv:    no
Requires:       libappindicator-gtk3
Requires:       gtk3
Requires:       gtk4 >= 4.14
Requires:       gobject-introspection
Requires:       libffi
Requires:       libadwaita >= 1.5
Requires:       nss
Requires:       nspr
Requires:       alsa-lib
Requires:       at-spi2-atk
Requires:       libdrm
Requires:       mesa-libgbm
Requires:       libX11
Requires:       libXcomposite
Requires:       libXdamage
Requires:       libXext
Requires:       libXfixes
Requires:       libXrandr
Requires:       libxcb
Requires:       libxkbcommon
Requires:       cups-libs
Requires:       dbus-libs
Requires:       glib2
Requires:       pango
Requires:       cairo
Requires:       libstdc++
Requires:       libgcc
Requires:       systemd-libs
Requires:       expat
Requires:       glibc >= 2.34
Requires:       xdg-utils

%description
Independent Node.js Amazon Music client with a native GTK4/libadwaita window.
CastLabs Electron/Chromium renders the web player off-screen inside the native window.
Includes integrated preferences, optional hardware acceleration and MPRIS.
An Amazon account, internet access and a working Widevine CDM are required
for protected playback. HD/Ultra HD availability depends on Amazon.

%prep
%setup -q

%build
# The verified Node.js and CastLabs Electron runtimes are in Source0.

%install
mkdir -p %{buildroot}/opt/%{name}
cp -a app %{buildroot}/opt/%{name}/
install -Dm755 packaging/amazon-music-linux %{buildroot}%{_bindir}/%{name}
install -Dm644 packaging/io.github.amzml.AmazonMusic.desktop %{buildroot}%{_datadir}/applications/io.github.amzml.AmazonMusic.desktop
install -Dm644 app/assets/io.github.amzml.AmazonMusic.svg %{buildroot}%{_datadir}/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/io.github.amzml.AmazonMusic.svg

install -Dm644 app/assets/io.github.amzml.AmazonMusic.png %{buildroot}%{_datadir}/icons/hicolor/512x512/apps/io.github.amzml.AmazonMusic.png

%files
%{_bindir}/%{name}
%{_datadir}/applications/io.github.amzml.AmazonMusic.desktop
%{_datadir}/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/io.github.amzml.AmazonMusic.svg
%{_datadir}/icons/hicolor/512x512/apps/io.github.amzml.AmazonMusic.png
%dir /opt/%{name}
/opt/%{name}/app
%changelog
* Tue Oct 27 2026 Amazon Music Linux contributors - 0.5.2-1
- Keep memory reclamation internal and automatic; remove menu and preferences controls.

* Tue Oct 27 2026 Amazon Music Linux contributors - 0.5.1-1
- Add manual and one-shot background memory reclamation without reloading playback.
- Release hidden GTK frames and shared-memory pages after capture pauses.
- Read software frames directly into native textures to reduce buffer duplication.

* Tue Oct 27 2026 Amazon Music Linux contributors - 0.5.0-1
- Rewrite the GTK4/libadwaita application and build tooling in Node.js.
- Keep one visible window, GPU textures, GNOME media controls and background audio.
- Bundle pinned Node.js and Electron runtimes; remove the Python dependency.

* Fri Oct 09 2026 Amazon Music Linux contributors - @VERSION@-1
- Import Electron GPU DMA-BUF textures directly into GTK without per-frame CPU readback.
- Preserve fractional touchpad scrolling and mark precise wheel input.
- Publish cached album artwork and implement MPRIS Next/Previous through MediaSession.

* Fri Oct 09 2026 Amazon Music Linux contributors - 0.4.2-1
- Observe detached audio and MediaSession metadata/actions for the GNOME media player.
- Deliver HiDPI bitmaps through leased shared-memory buffers at the active display refresh rate.
- Preserve pixel scrolling from touchpads and synchronize presentation with GTK.

* Fri Oct 09 2026 Amazon Music Linux contributors - 0.4.1-1
- Add optional background playback with a StatusNotifier tray menu.
- Publish the Amazon icon as the GNOME media-card artwork.

* Fri Oct 09 2026 Amazon Music Linux contributors - 0.4.0-1
- Keep the native GTK4/libadwaita window and replace CEF with hidden offscreen Electron.
- Preserve native theme, GPU preferences, MPRIS and completed Widevine registration.

* Fri Oct 09 2026 Amazon Music Linux contributors - 0.3.0-1
- Replace Electron with CEF and a native GTK4/libadwaita application window.
- Embed CEF off-screen frames, popup widgets and native input routing.
- Use native preferences, desktop appearance, GPU settings and MPRIS.
- Probe Widevine with EME instead of assuming DRM readiness.

* Fri Oct 09 2026 Amazon Music Linux contributors - 0.2.1-1
- Use the completed Widevine registration result to avoid repeated restart prompts.
- Follow the desktop appearance portal and live color scheme changes.
- Clear the inherited desktop identity on relaunch and retain diagnostic profiles.
* Fri Oct 09 2026 Amazon Music Linux contributors - 0.2.0-1
- Embed the player and preferences in a single Electron window.
- Persist the hardware acceleration preference with restart and software override.
- Keep MPRIS integration using a headless service.
* Fri Oct 09 2026 Amazon Music Linux contributors - 0.1.2-1
- Replace the app icon with a white Amazon smile on a blue background.
* Fri Oct 09 2026 Amazon Music Linux contributors - 0.1.1-1
- Use software rendering to avoid black player windows on Wayland.
- Display loading failures and allow retry; verify rendered pixels in smoke tests.
* Fri Oct 09 2026 Amazon Music Linux contributors - 0.1.0-1
- Initial GTK4/libadwaita and Electron client.
